{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":18,"code":"JOB","name":"Job","testament":"OT"},"chapter":8,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"JOB 8:1"},"Then answered Bildad the Shuhite, and said, ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"JOB 8:2"},"How long wilt thou speak these ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["things?"]}," and ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["how long shall "]},"the words of thy mouth be like a strong wind? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"JOB 8:3"},"Doth God pervert judgment? or doth the Almighty pervert justice? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"JOB 8:4"},"If thy children have sinned against him, and he have cast them away for their transgression; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"JOB 8:5"},"If thou wouldest seek unto God betimes, and make thy supplication to the Almighty; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"JOB 8:6"},"If thou ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["wert"]}," pure and upright; surely now he would awake for thee, and make the habitation of thy righteousness prosperous. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"JOB 8:7"},"Though thy beginning was small, yet thy latter end should greatly increase. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"JOB 8:8"},"For enquire, I pray thee, of the former age, and prepare thyself to the search of their fathers: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"JOB 8:9"},"(For we ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are but of"]}," yesterday, and know nothing, because our days upon earth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," a shadow:) ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"JOB 8:10"},"Shall not they teach thee, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," tell thee, and utter words out of their heart? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"JOB 8:11"},"Can the rush grow up without mire? can the flag grow without water? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"JOB 8:12"},"Whilst it ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," yet in his greenness, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," not cut down, it withereth before any ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["other"]}," herb. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"JOB 8:13"},"So ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," the paths of all that forget God; and the hypocrite’s hope shall perish: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"JOB 8:14"},"Whose hope shall be cut off, and whose trust ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["shall be"]}," a spider’s web. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"JOB 8:15"},"He shall lean upon his house, but it shall not stand: he shall hold it fast, but it shall not endure. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"JOB 8:16"},"He ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," green before the sun, and his branch shooteth forth in his garden. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"JOB 8:17"},"His roots are wrapped about the heap, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," seeth the place of stones. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:17"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"JOB 8:18"},"If he destroy him from his place, then ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it"]}," shall deny him, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["saying,"]}," I have not seen thee. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:18"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"19","sid":"JOB 8:19"},"Behold, this ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," the joy of his way, and out of the earth shall others grow. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:19"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"20","sid":"JOB 8:20"},"Behold, God will not cast away a perfect ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["man,"]}," neither will he help the evil doers: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:20"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"21","sid":"JOB 8:21"},"Till he fill thy mouth with laughing, and thy lips with rejoicing. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:21"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"22","sid":"JOB 8:22"},"They that hate thee shall be clothed with shame; and the dwelling place of the wicked shall come to nought. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 8:22"}]}]}
